{
 "id": "repair_default",
 "displayName": "Repair Default",
 "type": "Decoration",
 "kind": "Cell",
 "_note": "Repair-economy DATA row (owner ruling 2026-07-11), NOT a buildable structure: no visualPrefabPath (regressions skip it) and type Decoration maps to no build verb in build-categories.json, so it never appears in a palette. WallRepairController prices repair as damage-fraction x a structure's own catalog build cost in materials (wood/iron/food; crystals n",

            "ever charged); a structure with no materials cost row anywhere (runtime stations like the Apothecary, harvest sites) falls back to THIS row's repo.cost. Destroyed = 100% fraction = full cost = the Rebuild price. v42 (PROD-014 slice d, OWNER RULING 2026-08-26) adds repo.repairCrystalsPer -- the CRYSTALS-FOR-REPAIR exchange rate, 1.0 crystal per IRON, authored HERE and on no other row. It is a rate a player may opt into when a repair is refused for want of materials, NOT a cost slot: repo.cost.crystals stays 0 and WallRepairController.CostForFraction still emits zero crystals, so the ordinary WO-947 basket (regular = wood + iron) is untouched. perWood and perFood are 0 because the owner ruled ONE number and 0 means NOT CONVERTIBLE, never free. Keep the Resources + StreamingAssets copies byte-equal.",
   "repo": {
    "behaviorId": null,
    "buildCost": 0,
    "cost": {
     "wood": 120,
     "food": 0,
     "iron": 60,
     "crystals": 0
    },
    "repairCrystalsPer": {
     "perWood": 0,
     "perFood": 0,
     "perIron": 1.0
    },
    "navSurface": "None",
    "placement": {
     "mustSitOn": "Ground",
     "footprint": 1,
     "noOverlap": false,
     "checkAffordable": false
    }
   }
  }
 ],
 "_restoreGoldNote": "TIER-ONE PRODUCER RESTORE (owner ruling 2026-08-23): a DESTROYED tier-one producer is restored for GOLD ONLY, flat, dependent on nothing else. ⛔ THIS IS A NAMED EXCEPTION TO WO-753 (destroyed items never rebuild - build fresh at full cost); it is deliberate, not a contradiction, and exists because every tier-one producer is priced in the resource it PRODUCES (the armorer costs 280 iron to build the iron producer, the lumber mill 160 wood to build the wood producer). Without this the economy closes on itself: lose the building, lose the resource, cannot afford the building. Gold is UNCAPPED by design and drops from kills (3-120, median 18), so recovery is always reachable without another building. First placement stays FREE via freeBuildsUsed (save v32)."
}
",

